  "notes": [
    "Reflexive -IR verb with a dual stem change, following the same pattern as *sentir*, *preferir*, *mentir*: e→ie in the presente (all but nosotros/nosotras) and subjuntivo presente (all but nosotros/nosotras), plus e→i in the 3rd-person pretérito indefinido (se convirtió, se convirtieron) and in the nosotros/nosotras form of subjuntivo presente (nos convirtamos).",
    "Almost always used with \"en\": *convertirse en algo* (\"to become/turn into something\").",
    "Past participle is regular: **convertido**.",
    "Imperativo afirmativo reflexive pronouns attach to the end with a written accent to preserve stress (conviértete, conviértase, convirtámonos, conviértanse); imperativo negativo places them separately in front (no te conviertas...).",
    "*Se convirtió en el mejor de su clase.* (\"He became the best in his class.\")",
    "*El agua se convierte en hielo a cero grados.* (\"Water turns into ice at zero degrees.\")",
    "Related: *convertir* (non-reflexive, \"to convert/turn something into\"), *la conversión* (conversion, noun), *volverse*/*hacerse*/*llegar a ser* (related \"to become\" verbs, each with slightly different nuance)."
  ],
